From: OpenWrt E8450 investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: persist NETSYSv1 QDMA rate overrides

Turn the disposable NETSYSv1 QDMA rate-write probe into a stateful queue
shaper for lifecycle and Gate-E testing on MT7622. Store link speed,
requested override, and effective encoded rate for each of the 16 queues.
Serialize state and QTX_SCH writes, reapply state after DMA queue
initialization, and make DSA link notifications preserve active overrides.

A zero rate now disables the override and restores the latest driver
link-rate word instead of leaving the queue uncapped. Restrict the writable
interface to non-MT7621 NETSYSv1 layouts, reject trailing or overflowing
input, expose decoded state alongside raw register readback, and defer MMIO
writes while the frame-engine reset flag is set. Existing NETSYSv2/v3 and
MT7621 paths are unchanged.

This remains an experimental root-only debugfs control. It does not alter
PPE queue selection, WED, firewall offload, SQM, or per-packet processing.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt E8450 investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
